X_1(5) Sym^2 HOST (Beukers Thm 4; lambda_1=phi^5, lambda_2=phi^{-5} unit, c=-1, k=3)
  c = -1  =>  sigma_p = v_p(c) = 0 at EVERY prime (Cor 3.2 of CRYSTAL_THEOREM_F);
  lambda_2 is a unit  =>  the pure module Li_j(x/s) has v_p-slope v_p(lambda_2) = 0 too.
  Hence gamma_p = 0 at every prime and the adelic bound coincides with CDT's:
